      <p>Canadian buyers should avoid accepting vague descriptions such as “kraft bowl, premium quality” or “compostable cup.” The order must identify the exact material construction, capacity tolerance, coating type, colour standard, carton count, pallet arrangement and intended food application. If the package is designed for poutine, soup, oily noodles or hot beverages, testing conditions must reflect that use.</p>

